{
  "dom_id": "step-q42741",
  "name": "Question 19",
  "problem": "Let $V={R}_{1}[t]$ be the vector space of all polynomials of degree at most $1,$ equipped with the inner product\n\n$$\n\u27e8x(t),y(t)\u27e9=x(1)y(1)+x(2)y(2).\n$$\n\nNormalize the  vector  $p(t)=2+t.$",
  "worked_solution": "The norm of a vector $f(t)$ with respect to an inner product $\u27e8\\cdot ,\\cdot \u27e9$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\u2016p(t)\u2016=\\sqrt{\u27e8p(t),p(t)\u27e9}.\n$$\n\nSince $p(t)=2+t,$ we obtain\n\n$$\np(1)=3,\\,p(2)=4.\n$$\n\nComputing the inner product using our definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u27e8p(t),p(t)\u27e9 & =[p(1)]^{2}+[p(2)]^{2} \\\\  & ={3}^{2}+{4}^{2} \\\\  & =9+16 \\\\  & =25.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u2016p(t)\u2016 & =\\sqrt{25}=5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo normalize the vector $p(t)$, we divide $p(t)$ by its norm $\u2016p(t)\u2016:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(t) & =\\frac{p(t)}{\u2016p(t)\u2016} \\\\  & =\\frac{2+t}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(2+t)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
